Network Interface Configuration:
​Configure and verify network interfaces across public and private channels on all cluster nodes. Ensure dedicated allocation for client access/SCAN and cluster interconnect routing. Validate active status and link speeds for zero-drop communication.
​DNS & Host File Configuration:
​Map public, private (-priv), and SCAN hostnames to their respective IP addresses across /etc/hosts and central DNS. Ensure a single SCAN address resolves to all cluster node IPs as required for Oracle RAC load balancing. Perform reverse lookup tests to confirm network alignment.
​Time Synchronization (NTP/Chrony):
​Configure and synchronize chrony/NTP services across all cluster nodes with the central time authority. Ensure minimal time drift between nodes to maintain RAC cluster health and voting integrity. Verify active sync status prior to database deployment.
​Firewall & Port Rules:
​Disable firewalld or open specific RAC communication ports (e.g., 1521 for listeners, 6200–6299 for interconnects). Validate open state across nodes to prevent inter-node traffic blockage. Ensure security exceptions are properly documented.
​Disable SELinux:
​Set SELinux mode to permissive/disabled within /etc/selinux/config. Ensure system enforcement is completely bypassed to prevent permission conflicts during Oracle RAC installation. Confirm persistent setting post-reboot.
​SSH Port & Authentication Setup:
​Update /etc/ssh/sshd_config to enable dedicated administrative ports (22 and 27041) and permit password authentication. Restart SSH daemons to apply changes cleanly. Confirm login connectivity across target nodes.
​B. Shared Storage Setup
​Shared Block Storage & Multipathing:
​Provision shared block storage accessible across all three cluster nodes utilizing MPIO or iSCSI. Configure DM-Multipath on all nodes to provide storage redundant pathing. Validate multi-path status and device mapping stability.
​ASM Disk & Layout Configuration:
​Partition and label shared disks dedicated for Oracle ASM deployment (OCR/Voting and DATA/RECO disk groups). Allocate at least 3 distinct partitions/disks for OCR/Voting to ensure quorum. Verify disk visibility and read/write consistency across all nodes.
