​Resource Limits Setup:
​Configure system resource limits in /etc/security/limits.conf for oracle and grid OS users. Define soft and hard limits for open file descriptors, processes, and stack sizes. Verify applied limits by testing user sessions.
​Resolv.conf / Host File / NTP Rules:
​Apply mandatory network resolution and time configs within /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hosts, and time sync services. Confirm proper domain lookup sequences and consistent local resolution. Validate end-to-end communication readiness across nodes.
​Server-to-Server SSH Passwordless Setup:
​Establish passwordless SSH connectivity for oracle and grid users across all cluster nodes. Exchange public keys and test user access via SSH without prompting for credentials. Verify cluster management utility capability.
​Mount NFS Storage & System Entries:
​Mount required Enterprise NFS shares to local directory structures for installation binaries and backups. Apply default umask configurations and grant necessary sudoers privileges for system administrative roles. Validate file system access permissions.
​Local & Shared Disks Creation:
​Initialize local filesystems alongside shared disk groups required for database files. Set correct device ownership (grid:asmadmin / oracle:oinstall) and permissions (0660). Confirm disk initialization across every cluster member node.
